<b>Ougi
Kinoa</b>

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:48.830
Bubuki
"Himekiri" "Hoemaru"

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:49.790
<b>Taneome
Shizuru</b>

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:49.790
<b>Oubu's Right Foot</b>

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:49.790
Bubuki "Tsurarai"

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:51.250
<b>Nono
Hiiragi</b>

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:51.250
<b>Oubu's Left Foot</b>

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:51.250
<b></b>Bubuki "Iwatooshi"

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.000
<b>Oubu's
Heart</b>

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.000
<b>Kazuki
Azuma</b>

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:53.590
<b>Taneome
Shizuru</b>

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:53.590
<b>Asabuki
Kogane</b>

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:53.590
<b>Kazuki
Azuma</b>

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:53.590
<b>Ougi
Kinoa</b>

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:53.590
<b>Nono
Hiiragi</b>

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.260
<b>Matobai
Shuusaku</b>

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.380
<b>Arabashiri
Souya</b>

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.840
<b>Tsuwabuki
Akihito</b>

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.050
<b>Hazama
Zetsubi</b>

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.180
<b>Banryuu
Reoko</b>

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.430
<b>Tsuwabuki
Akihito</b>

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.430
<b>Matobai
Shuusaku</b>

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.430
<b>Banryuu
Reoko</b>

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.430
<b>Arabashiri
Souya</b>

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.430
<b>Hazama
Zetsubi</b>

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.980
<b><i>Bubuki/Buranki</i></b>

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.510
Oh, yeah... I haven't really 
heard all of your names yet.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:04.860
Huh? If you're gonna ask people's 
names, give your own first.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.040
Sorry...

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.290
I'm Kazuki Azuma.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.910
It's written with the characters 
for "one hope" and "east."

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.790
I'm Kinoa... Ougi Kinoa.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.230
This is...

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.920
I am a Shizuru. As yet I have no name.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.390
Taneome Shizuru.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:23.650
Meow, meow.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.530
Nice to meet you.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.850
What's nice about it?

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.370
Do you understand the situation we're in?

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.090
Kazuki Migiwa is dead.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:33.800
We worked so hard to get our hands on Oubu,

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.890
and now there's no point in going 
to the Buranki nest anymore...

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:37.930
She's not dead.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:38.860
What?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.990
My mom is not dead.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.580
What are you basing that on?

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.840
That girl said one Buranki fell.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:50.740
If my mom was dead,
there would be a lot more than one.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.170
I get it! That's true!

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:55.730
They might come falling down any time now.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:04:00.160
Look, first off, are you <i>really</i>
 gonna believe Reoko?

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.300
W-Well...

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.130
Her name was Reoko?

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:07.210
Banryuu Reoko.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:09.530
She is our real enemy,

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.890
and an actual witch.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.140
An actual witch?

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:16.310
A-chan! We're here! This is it!

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:17.890
A station?

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.940
Yeah! There's someone here who can help us!

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.330
Help us? I dunno about that.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.650
There you go again, Hii-kun!

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.210
We can finally catch our breaths.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.370
And I'm so hungry, I can barely walk.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.850
Come on, let's go.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.760
Hi hi, Horino-san!

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.810
Oh...

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.680
You made it back alive.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.850
You took so long,
 I thought you'd been killed.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.500
Well, a lot of things happened 
that we weren't counting on.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.240
And what about Oubu?

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.230
We got it!

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.450
Good work, good work.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.880
Are you Azuma-kun?

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.580
I'm Horino.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.270
Whoa!

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:21.840
Yes... I'm glad you all met 
up with him as planned.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:25.260
We couldn't beat Reoko, though.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.430
Don't get greedy.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:31.850
It's more than enough that you all made 
it back alive from a battle with Entei.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.140
Entei...

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.640
You mean that red Buranki?

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:41.680
Yep. Entei fell down to this 
world long ago, just like Oubu.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.440
You saw lots of them in the Buranki 
nest when you were little, didn't you?

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.400
Treasure Island...

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.320
Huh?

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:52.130
My mother called that 
place "Treasure Island."

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:55.040
The Buranki nest is Treasure Island, eh?

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.790
I just don't get how geniuses think.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.820
Well, no matter.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:04.000
What sort of person is the 
genius's son, I wonder?

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:08.800
Those aren't the eyes of 
an activist or militant.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.010
But there's...

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.690
What is it?

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.980
Something even deeper in this boy.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.810
We've rested enough!

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.940
We need to take off for the Buranki nest!

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.690
Aw, we're leaving already?

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.560
We can't afford to dilly-dally around here!

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:28.180
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.610
You could take it easy just for today.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.220
No, thanks.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.910
Hanging around someone who ran 
from battle will rot me, too.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.740
Hii-kun, that's mean!

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.080
Horino-san is still an activist... 
for loco moco bowls!

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.560
For a secret menu?!

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:45.940
You mean "anti-government"!
All those have in common is the "m"!

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:48.610
I'm so hungry, I couldn't help it!

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:52.720
Oh, it's fine. He's right 
that I left the battle.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.320
And that's why I can't 
stand that part of you.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.400
Horino-san, I'm borrowing your kitchen.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.190
Kinoa! What are you doing?!

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.680
What am I doing? What does it look like?

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:07.310
One,

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.360
I'm so hungry, everything's pissing me off!

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:09.360
two,

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.200
Get in my way and I'll beat your ass!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.200
three...

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.660
I can't let her beat me!

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.630
Horirin, where's your miso?

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:23.040
I don't have any miso. 
I don't eat miso soup.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:27.730
What? Oh, all right...
I guess I'll use sugar instead.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.400
You're all so...

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.430
Fine, do whatever!

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:37.720
No delicacy at all.
Did a man cook this or what?

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.700
Don't eat it, then.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.890
I never said I didn't want any.

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:44.080
Let's dig in!

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.200
Delicious!

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.990
Well? How is it?

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.440
Damn it... It's good.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:00.080
Oh, Shizuru, I promised I'd let 
you eat lots of grass, didn't I?

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:05.550
Here! My special menu item:
grass bowl with extra cilantro!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.530
It's like a mountain of grass!

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:12.000
Okay, once we've eaten and rested,

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.620
we'll take off before dawn.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.350
Okay, fine, Leader.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:20.110
It might not make sense to you 
since you ran off overseas,

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:21.990
but this country has been ruled

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:25.060
from the shadows by the fear of 
Entei for the last ten years.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:26.940
Ten years?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.730
No one can defy Reoko, nor do they try to.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.050
But there is a way to defeat her and Entei.

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:38.830
We just have to bring Migiwa back from the 
Buranki nest and have her fight Reoko.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:43.190
Kazuki Migiwa has beaten Reoko before.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.190
My mom beat Reoko?

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.390
Is that true, Horirin?

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:51.010
Yes, before all of you were born.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:04.440
Azuma, I'm going to show 
you something you'll like.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:11.890
You need to know more about your 
mother, the Buranki, and Reoko.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.950
<b>I</b>

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.950
<b>II</b>

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.950
<b>III</b>

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:26.080
Do you think you could help us out a little?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.880
Unlike you, we've got a quota to meet.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:33.050
Ah, there's no time. There's just no time.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:35.550
Damned dog of Reoko...

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:41.100
I may be a dog, but I'm a clever,
ferocious guard dog.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.640
<b>III</b>

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:45.640
Should be any time now...

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:48.370
Ah, yeah, we've got him.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:52.810
Hey, what are you doing? He's getting away!

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:58.660
A Bubuki!

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.700
It was in stealth mode?

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.990
Now you've met your quota.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.300
We've got an unregistered one!

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:09.250
Get the officer on duty to the 
location and restrain the suspect!

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:13.500
It's a damn tough world for 
a Bubuki user to live in.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.460
Hey!

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.360
How did you find it?

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:18.520
The Bubuki was in stealth mode.

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:23.440
There are all kinds of ways 
to identify a Bubuki user.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:24.470
Want to know them?

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.140
Yes, please tell me.

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:28.160
Who, me?

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:29.850
I don't think so.

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:33.860
I see, I see.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:37.240
So that's where you're hiding.

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:40.570
Just wait right there, kitten.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:45.080
<b>Episode 3
Heart and Limbs</b>

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:54.340
So Righty-chan's real name is Raijoudou?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.740
Sounds way too snooty, right?

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.550
Does it <i>look</i> like a Raijoudou?

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:02.640
An ancestor of mine gave it that 
name a long, long time ago.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:05.460
A long, long time ago?

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:07.220
I see...

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:10.640
What's this?

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:16.030
All the information's that ever been
collected about Bubuki is gathered here.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:18.910
Don't worry.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:22.240
None of the Bubuki here will ever move again.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.320
What?

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:26.040
<b>Cores</b>

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.180
So long as their eyeballs aren't destroyed,

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:29.150
they can infinitely regenerate
any damage done to their bodies.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:30.330
Then why...

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:32.800
They have no masters.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:33.420
Huh?

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:38.280
The Bubuki you all use are 
the Buranki Oubu's heart,

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:42.840
right hand, left hand, 
right foot, and left foot.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:45.010
The five Bubuki belong to, respectively,

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:45.950
the Kazuki,

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:46.810
Asabuki,

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:47.680
Ougi,

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:48.600
Taneomi,

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.630
and Nono families.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:53.630
They've been handed down in 
your families for generations.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:58.530
In other words, the Bubuki have taken
people from those bloodlines as masters.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:02.200
Why do the Bubuki make humans their masters?

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.410
I don't have a clue.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:07.310
Your mom might know, though.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:08.860
My mom?

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:12.160
Since it's said that your mom

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:18.020
has all the information contained 
in these books within her mind.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.820
We call it the Kazuki Library.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:22.880
It's here now due to the circumstances,

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:27.540
but they've been handed down in your 
family for generations, Azuma.

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:33.310
The Kazuki and Banryuu families,
which each inherited a Buranki's heart,

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.320
have always been at odds with each other,

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:40.070
acting behind the scenes of this
world's history of war and strife.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:45.950
So why did Reoko step front and center
 onto the stage of history 24 years ago?

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:49.830
Nobody knows, to this day.

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:54.430
But Oubu, under Kazuki Migiwa's control,

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:57.550
engaged Entei and Reoko in Ueno

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:00.450
and defeated it,
bringing the situation under control.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:05.710
After that, Migiwa ascended 
to the Buranki nest.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.590
The world was at peace 
after that, for a while.

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:14.320
Until ten years ago, when a Buranki 
suddenly fell from the sky,

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:17.500
and Reoko and Entei came back.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:22.820
There's something I have to 
ask the son of Kazuki Migiwa.

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:26.110
Why did you and Oubu fall?

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:32.240
Why did the other eight Buranki fall?

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:40.600
Didn't Migiwa go up to the nest to ensure 
no more Buranki would come here?

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:43.940
So why? Why did those Buranki fall?!

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:46.430
Hii-kun!

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:48.150
Step outside.

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:51.420
I'll ask again.

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:54.810
Why did the Buranki fall 
on that day ten years ago?

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:57.340
Answer me!

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:58.810
It was my fault.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.730
What do you mean?

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:03.190
I'm sorry. I can't give much 
more detail than that.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:08.030
Well, that's fine. At least I 
know one thing for sure now.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:19.620
You aren't the right one 
to wield Oubu's heart.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:20.880
Give it to me!

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.550
Y-You sure we shouldn't stop him?

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.630
Now, just be quiet and watch.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:30.160
I don't know if I'm the right one 
to wield Oubu's heart or not.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:31.540
But...

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:36.020
I have to go to Treasure Island 
on Oubu to save my mom.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.280
Even more reason to give it to me.

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:42.600
I'll control Oubu and take 
you to the Buranki nest!

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.650
I can't give you the heart.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.220
Well, then...

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.360
I'll take it by force!

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:52.570
A-cha—

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:55.240
Go! Go!

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:57.580
Now, hang on. It's just getting good.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:17.020
What's your problem? Fight me!

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.900
Sorry about before.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:27.190
Did that hurt you, too?

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.840
What are you mumbling about?

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.730
Hiiragi! You're taking this too far!

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:47.520
So long as the heart treats the 
other parts as mere limbs,

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:50.170
Oubu's true power will never awaken.

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:54.430
The relationship between the heart and limbs 
is not that of a king and his subjects.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:56.760
So what is it, then?

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:58.300
Who knows?

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.600
You guys have to forge that 
relationship yourselves,

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:05.020
exchanging both blows and words.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:07.480
Ah, youth...

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:12.030
The heart is the only connection I have...

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:14.280
To my mother...

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.260
To my family.

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:20.040
So I can't give it away. Ever.

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:22.390
Hiiragi...

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:25.900
Let's go to Treasure Island together.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:36.920
I'm sick of hearing about 
your mom, you mama's boy!

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.130
Useless piece of crap!

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.850
Are you okay, A-chan?

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:47.220
Yeah.

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:50.560
Listen, Hii-kun isn't a bad guy.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.650
He wants to change this 
world more than anyone,

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:55.350
for his dad.

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:56.700
His dad?

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:06.750
Forget forging a relationship.
I think theirs just got even worse.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:07.840
I know!

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:09.810
A bath!

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:13.500
What they need is a little 
open communication!

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:14.390
Am I right?

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:16.600
Well, a bath would be nice.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.470
The one at our hideout is kinda...

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:21.350
Well, then, enough chattering! 
Let's get it ready!

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:30.900
Man, this is boring. Boring, boring, boring.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:34.050
Hey, up for a little wager?

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.910
What, didn't you hear me?

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.760
I asked if you wanted to make a bet.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:42.410
I'm very sorry. I'm on duty.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.120
Don't be such a stiff.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:49.980
It's just a little bet on 
which one wakes up first.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:52.470
Which one... wakes up first?

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:53.730
Yeah.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:58.180
Which will wake up first, Reoko-sama 
or the headless Buranki?

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:01.560
I think it'll be Reoko-sama, of course.

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:04.530
Yeah, that's what I figured.

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:07.190
That's what we need to happen, isn't it?

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:12.190
If the headless Buranki 
wakes up first, no one here

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:15.110
will get to go home alive.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.580
<b>Kaboom</b>

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:28.500
I'm surprised there's a bath here.

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:35.590
Here, Righty-chan. Scrub, scrub, scrub!

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:37.010
So which one do you think 
should wield Oubu's heart?

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:40.220
And now for this side. Scrub, scrub, scrub!

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:39.430
Azuma or Hiiragi?

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:45.390
Huh? I can't just pick one 
of them out of the blue...

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.640
<b>Peek and Die!!</b>

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:48.640
"Out of the blue" isn't 
the problem, you idiot!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.170
I'd be fine with Hiiragi. He's our leader.

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:56.940
Well, I always thought you had 
something special, Kinoa.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:19:00.150
Guys like him are so easy to handle.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:03.490
All you have to do is call him "Leader."

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.250
I can hear you, Kinoa!

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:08.750
Oh, could you hear me?

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:18.470
So you want to change the 
world for your dad, Hiiragi?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:19.730
Huh?

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.770
Kogane-chan told me earlier.

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:24.660
She's such a bigmouth.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:33.200
A long time ago, my dad fought alongside 
Migiwa and Kogane's parents.

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:35.940
And they defeated Entei.

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:37.850
It was incredible.

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.550
He was basically a hero.

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:43.340
But now he skulks around 
away from human eyes,

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:45.930
drowning himself in liquor every day.

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:48.450
It's so pathetic, I can't stand to watch.

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:53.960
So I'm going to defeat Reoko 
and open my dad's eyes.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:58.640
I've said too much.

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:01.290
This has nothing to do with you.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.610
Hey, did you hear that?

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:15.520
Yeah.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:16.980
Someone's outside.

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:18.820
An enemy?

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:22.490
There should be a redoubled guard 
against intruders out there.

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:38.380
Hello!

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:42.020
Hey there, heart.

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:43.720
I'm here to crush you.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:46.100
A-chan?

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:47.600
Kogane-chan!

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:48.970
Stay away!

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:53.100
Hey, little girl. You look 
cute when you're all sleepy.

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:55.560
I'll kill you!

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:02.360
Oh, how scary.

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:20.000
Why won't they come off?

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:37.960
Dad?

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:44.090
Dad, are you okay?

00:21:44.970 --> 00:21:46.660
Dad!

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.980
Please, help my dad!

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:52.590
You have to help my dad!

00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:00.750
I'll gouge out your everything!

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:04.670
Your eyes, your nose,
your throat, and your guts!

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:08.350
I'll gouge them out with this very hand!
